  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is Isabella Johansson with zip code 32286. They want to find their order that was sent to Texas by accident. They need the tracking number and return all items except the pet bed, refund to their Amex credit card. They don't remember the order number.\n\nFirst, I found their user ID using the name and zip. Now, I need to get their user details to see their orders. So next step is to call get_user_details with the user_id isabella_johansson_2152. That will show their orders. Once I have the orders, I can look for the one that was sent to Texas. Once I find the order ID, I can get the tracking number from the order details. Then, check if the order is delivered or pending. Since they want to return items, it's probably delivered. Then, use return_delivered_order_items for the items except the pet bed. Also, need to confirm the payment method ID for Amex. Maybe check their payment methods through user details. Need to make sure each step is done one at a time. Let's start with getting user details.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"isabella_johansson_2152\"}}\n",
